<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates sideways in liquid market.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates sideways in liquid market.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The two and twelve-month Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were slightly lower, while the rest were unchanged, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's just sideways. There's really not much change in views since last week,&quot; a foreign bank trader said.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't expect rates to move up. The market is very liquid,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The Central Bank, however, had placed a floor on rates at an overnight borrowing rate of 10.5 percent, dealers said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  FEB 12		 FEB 11</p>
<p>    1 W		9  7/8		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    2 W		9  7/8		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/16		10  1/16</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/16		10  1/8</p>
<p>    3 M		10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    6 M		10  3/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  3/8		 10  7/16</p>
<p>    VAL		13-Feb		  12-Feb</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
